@startuml WorkStealingBulkHeadedScheduler
title Work-Stealing, Bulkheaded, Time-Bound-Priority Scheduler\nInternal design of the "gRPC Server" containers (aih / csj / hba) from ContainerDiagram.puml

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<external>> #D9D9D9
  BackgroundColor<<pool>> #E8F4FA
  BackgroundColor<<queue>> #FFF3CD
  BackgroundColor<<selector>> #FDE9D9
  BackgroundColor<<worker>> #D9EAD3
  BorderColor black
}

rectangle "Updates" <<external>> as Updates
rectangle "Research" <<external>> as Research

package "Resource-execution boundary" {

  rectangle "Local Chrome Pool  (hba / provider='local')\nsize = BrowserConfig.MaxConcurrentProcesses" <<pool>> as ChromePool {
    rectangle "Updates queue" <<queue>> as CQ_Updates
    rectangle "Research queue" <<queue>> as CQ_Research

    rectangle "Next-task selection, checked by every idle worker:\n1. own local deque non-empty? serve it (LIFO, cache-hot, lock-free)\n2. else: aging check — oldest Research item's deadline elapsed? serve it now\n3. else: Updates queue non-empty? serve it\n4. else: Research queue non-empty? serve it\n5. else: steal from a peer worker's local deque (a few passes) → park" <<selector>> as Selector

    rectangle "Worker 1\n(lock-free local deque)" <<worker>> as CW1
    rectangle "Worker 2\n(lock-free local deque)" <<worker>> as CW2

    CQ_Updates --> Selector
    CQ_Research --> Selector
    Selector --> CW1
    Selector --> CW2
    CW1 <-> CW2 : idle peer steals\nfrom busy peer's deque

    note right of CQ_Research
      Deadline set once, at enqueue:
      deadline = arrival + T − jitter.
      jitter is drawn independently per
      item from a single, PCG-seeded
      generator shared by every submitter
      to this queue, reusing the same lock
      that already serializes enqueue —
      it adds no separate point of
      contention. This staggers when a
      batch's items individually become
      eligible, instead of all becoming
      eligible at once — deadline never
      exceeds T, so the "waits at most T"
      bound is unchanged.
    end note
  }

  rectangle "2Captcha Hosted Browser Pool  (hba / provider='2captcha')\nsize = Api2CaptchaConfig.BrowserMaxConcurrentSessions" <<pool>> as CaptchaPool
  rectangle "LLM Pool  (aih.SuggestConfiguration + csj.judgeVerifiedContent)\nsize = LLM concurrency budget (not resource-capped today)" <<pool>> as LLMPool

  note bottom of CaptchaPool
    Same internal structure as the Local Chrome
    Pool: one queue per caller, the same
    aging + priority selection, and its own
    fixed-size set of workers with local deques
    that steal from each other, not from
    the Local Chrome Pool.
  end note

  note bottom of LLMPool
    Same internal structure. csj is only ever
    called *by* aih (see SequenceDiagram-updates
    -grpc.puml) — it is not a separate entry
    point, so it shares aih's pool rather than
    getting its own.
  end note
}

rectangle "Headless Chrome Fleet" <<external>> as ChromeFleet
rectangle "2captcha" <<external>> as TwoCaptcha
rectangle "AI Provider" <<external>> as AIProvider

Updates --> ChromePool
Research --> ChromePool
Updates --> CaptchaPool
Research --> CaptchaPool
Updates --> LLMPool
Research --> LLMPool

ChromePool --> ChromeFleet : CDP
CaptchaPool --> TwoCaptcha : API
LLMPool --> AIProvider : API

legend right
  |= Acronym / term |= Meaning |
  | csj | Content Service Judge — judges extracted content as substantive vs. junk (called internally by aih only) |
  | aih | AI Helper — LLM-driven auto-configuration of a new crawl source |
  | hba | Headless Browser Abstraction — chromedp / 2Captcha-backed page scraping |
  | CDP | Chrome DevTools Protocol |
  | T | Aging threshold — the maximum time a queued Research item can wait before being served ahead of backlog |
  | jitter | Independent per-item random offset subtracted from T at enqueue, so a batch's items don't all become eligible simultaneously |
end legend

@enduml
